  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_003: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted → 0.639 acc), evidence is extremely sparse. The most critical architectural decision in a multimodal model is how the two modalities are combined. config_008 is a clean single-variable A/B test: it changes only the fusion method from weighted to concat while holding all other settings identical (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool). This directly clarifies whether a learned weighted combination or a simple concatenation (letting the downstream classifier learn the interaction) is more effective. Understanding the fusion strategy early is high-value because it is a binary choice that will inform all subsequent multimodal experiments, and a small improvement here compounds across the remaining 8 experiments. It is the best use of experiment 2 because it reduces the most fundamental uncertainty with minimal confounding."
}

